This isn't really a bug in the JIT IMO. The problem is there is no synchronization in the code above. The JIT just exposes it as there might be a double check for _CHECK_PERIODIC (one in the interpreter, then once again entering JUMP_BACKWARD).

If you revert back to an old Python version (3.10 or 3.9, I don't remember), you'll get the same crash as well.

@markshannon WDYT?
